      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SEBASTIANS WAITING (2) has won a trial since manners let him down when tackling a G2 in Sydney last start. Overcame a second row draw for a resuming win at Bendigo two back and he gets a good barrier so has winning claims if he gets it right. KEAYANG GYPSY (6) resumes after great success last prep, winning on seven occasions. Strikes at 50 per cent at this circuit and distance and was readied with a trial win so is likely to run a big race to kick off the campaign. ALDEBARAN ABEL (4) didn't do a bad job from the back row last time and had recorded a string of top-four results prior. Worth another chance returning to the front line. UNCLAD (7) draws much wider than in his resuming win but he'll strip fitter and that victory took his record at this circuit and distance to two from two so respect.",
